<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>8.8.3: Factoring Quadratic Equations without a Linear Term</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02217</md:content-id>
    <md:title>8.8.3: Factoring Quadratic Equations without a Linear Term</md:title>
    <md:uuid>7b2c210f-4bf1-480b-8195-2ab31c9b348a</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Activity</title>
<para>In questions 1 - 2, each row of the table contains a pair of equivalent expressions.</para>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Convert the factored form expression to the standard form.</para>
    <para>If you get stuck, consider drawing a diagram.</para>
    <table class="os-raise-midsizetable">
      <thead>
        <row>
          <entry><emphasis>
            Factored form
          </emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>
            Standard form
          </emphasis></entry></row>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <row>
          <entry>
            \((x − 10)(x + 10)\)
          </entry>
          <entry> </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry>
            \((2x + 1)(2x − 1)\)
          </entry>
          <entry> </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry>
            \((4 − x)(4 + x)\)
          </entry>
          <entry> </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry>
            \((c + \frac{2}{5})(c − \frac{2}{5})\)
          </entry>
          <entry> </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry>
            \((x + 5)(x + 5)\)
          </entry>
          <entry> </entry>
        </row>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    
  <para>Write down your answers, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answers:</para>
  <table class="os-raise-midsizetable">
    <thead>
      <row>
        <entry><emphasis>
          Factored form
        </emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>
          Standard form
        </emphasis></entry></row>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <row>
        <entry>
          \((x − 10)(x + 10)\)
        </entry>
        <entry>
          \(x^2 − 100\)
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          \((2x + 1)(2x − 1)\)
        </entry>
        <entry>
          \(4x^2− 1\)
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          \((4 − x)(4 + x)\)
        </entry>
        <entry>
          \(16 − x^2\)

        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          \((c + \frac {2}{5})(c − \frac {2}{5})\)
        </entry>
        <entry>
          \(c^2 − \frac {4}{25}\)

        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          \((x + 5)(x + 5)\)
        </entry>
        <entry>
          \(x^2+ 10x + 25\)

        </entry>
      </row>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</solution></exercise>
</example>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Convert the standard form expression to the factored form.</para>
    <para>If you get stuck, consider drawing a diagram. (HINT: One of the expressions does not convert.)</para>
    <table class="os-raise-midsizetable">
      <thead>
        <row>
          <entry><emphasis>
            Factored form
          </emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>
            Standard form
          </emphasis></entry></row>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <row>
          <entry> </entry>
          <entry>
            \(x^2 − 81\)
          </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry> </entry>
          <entry>
            \(49 − y^2\)
          </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry> </entry>
          <entry>
            \(9z^2 − 16\)
          </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry> </entry>
          <entry>
            \(25t^2− 81\)
          </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry> </entry>
          <entry>
            \(\frac {49}{16} − d^2\)
          </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry> </entry>
          <entry>
            \(x^2− 6\)
          </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry> </entry>
          <entry>
            \(x^2 + 100\)
          </entry>
        </row>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    
  <para>Write down your answers, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answers:</para>
  <table class="os-raise-midsizetable">
    <thead>
      <row>
        <entry><emphasis>
          Factored form
        </emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>
          Standard form
        </emphasis></entry></row>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <row>
        <entry>
          \((x − 9)(x + 9)\)
        </entry>
        <entry>
          \(x^2 − 81\)
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          \((7 − y)(7 + y)\)
        </entry>
        <entry>
          \(49 − y^2\)
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          \((3z + 4)(3z − 4)\)
        </entry>
        <entry>
          \(9z^2 − 16\)
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          \((5t + 9)(5t − 9)\)
        </entry>
        <entry>
          \(25t^2− 81\)
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          \((\frac {7}{4} − d)(\frac {7}{4} + d)\)
        </entry>
        <entry>
          \(\frac {49}{16} − d^2\)
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          \((x − \sqrt{6})(x + \sqrt{6})\)
        </entry>
        <entry>
          \(x^2− 6\)
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          prime
        </entry>
        <entry>
          \(x^2 + 100\)
        </entry>
      </row>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  
</solution></exercise>
</example>
